{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"To factor means to rewrite an expression as a product. Let's try dividing the expression $99-45f+36b$ by each factor.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"####Factoring out $9$\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}99-45f+36b\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=9\\left(\\dfrac{99-45f+36b}{9}\\right)\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=9\\left(\\dfrac{99}{9}-\\dfrac{45f}{9}+\\dfrac{36b}{9}\\right) \\\\\\\\\n\u0026=9(11-5f+4b)\n\\end{align}$\n\nYes, $99-45f+36b$ is equivalent to $9(11-5f+4b)$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"####Factoring out $3$\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}99-45f+36b\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=3\\left(\\dfrac{99-45f+36b}{3}\\right)\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=3\\left(\\dfrac{99}{3}-\\dfrac{45f}{3}+\\dfrac{36b}{3}\\right) \\\\\\\\\n\u0026=3(33-15f+12b)\n\\end{align}$\n\nWe see that $99-45f+36b$ is equivalent to $3(33-15f+12b)$, not to $3(33-15+12)$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"####Factoring out $11$\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}99-45f+36b\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=11\\left(\\dfrac{99-45f+36b}{11}\\right)\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=11\\left(\\dfrac{99}{11}-\\dfrac{45f}{11}+\\dfrac{36b}{11}\\right) \\\\\\\\\n\u0026=11\\left(9-\\dfrac{45}{11}f+\\dfrac{36}{11}b\\right)\n\\end{align}$\n\nNo, $99-45f+36b$ is *not* equivalent to $11(9-4f+3b)$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"The following expressions are equivalent to $99-45f+36b$:\n\n- $9(11-5f+4b)$\n- $3(33-15f+12b)$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"**Factor $99-45f+36b$ to identify the equivalent expressions.**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"clue":"This expression is equivalent to $99-45f+36b$.","content":"$9(11-5f+4b)$","correct":true},{"clue":"This expression is equivalent to $99-45+36$.","content":"$3(33-15+12)$","correct":false},{"clue":"This expression is equivalent to $99-44f+33b$.","content":"$11(9-4f+3b)$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false},{"clue":"This expression is equivalent to $99-45f+36b$.","content":"$3(33-15f+12b)$","correct":true,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false}],"countChoices":true,"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":true,"randomize":false},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
